==German==

===Etymology===
From the sour taste of pure oxygen on the tongue, loan translation of French ''[[oxygène]]'' < Greek-Latin ''[[oxygenium]]'' "acid-maker".

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈzawɐʃtɔf]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-Sauerstoff.ogg|Audio (Austria)}}

===Noun===
{{infl|de|noun|g=m}}

# [[oxygen]]

====Usage notes====
* '''Sauerstoff''' [[tanken]] - to breathe fresh air (to go outside and "tank oxygen")

====Synonyms====
* [[Atemluft]] (breathing air)

====Coordinate terms====
* {{sense|Chemical Element}} Previous: [[Stickstoff]]. Next: [[Fluor]]

====Related terms====
* [[sauer]]
* [[Stoff]]
* [[Sauerstoffflasche]], [[Sauerstoffmangel]], [[Sauerstoffmaske]], [[Sauerstoffzelt]]

